{"`getBouncyCastleProvider()` returns the default JKS keystore provider (typically SUN), not a BouncyCastle provider. `KeyStore.getInstance(KeyStore.getDefaultType()).getProvider()` resolves to whichever provider backs the default keystore type, which is unrelated to BouncyCastle. If this simple provider intentionally has no BC dependency, consider returning `null` or throwing `UnsupportedOperationException` instead of returning a misleading provider instance.": 0.9379488229751587, "These two `ASN1Encoder.create().write(...)` calls are dead code \u2014 they allocate encoders, write to their internal streams, and the results are immediately discarded. The actual encoding is done in the subsequent `return` statement. Remove these lines.": 0.878237247467041, "Adding a non-default method to a public interface is a breaking API change for external implementors. Provide a default implementation (e.g., returning `0`) to maintain backward compatibility, consistent with how `ProviderFactory.order()` is declared in this codebase.": 0.9684199690818787, "The single P-256 key pair is reused for all three algorithm tests. `testES384` and `testES512` never exercise realistic P-384/P-521 signature component sizes because the R and S values from the P-256 key are far shorter than what those algorithms produce in practice. Generate algorithm-appropriate key pairs so the DER\u2194concatenatedRS conversion is tested with correctly-sized components.": 0.7969099283218384, "Indefinite-length encoding (0x80) returns -1, but no caller handles this value. `readInteger()` will throw `NegativeArraySizeException`, `readSequence()` silently returns an empty list, and `readNext()` reads the wrong number of bytes. Since DER disallows indefinite-length, throw an `IOException` here instead of returning -1.": 0.890384316444397, "`debugf` treats its first argument as a format string. Since `builder` contains arbitrary class names (not a format pattern), use `logger.debug(builder.toString())` to avoid a potential `MissingFormatArgumentException` if a class name contains `%`.": 0.8957963585853577, "Trailing \", \" after the last provider name in the log message. Consider using `String.join` or adding a conditional separator to avoid the dangling comma.": 0.3014231026172638, "Non-standard modifier order: `static public` should be `public static` per Java conventions (JLS \u00a78.4.3).": 0.3338916599750519}